<title>UK: Reuters' 5th ex-UK Asia/Mideast air cargo report.</title>
<headline>Reuters' 5th ex-UK Asia/Mideast air cargo report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK to the Middle East/Asia/Australasia GBP air cargo market rates per kg for a 100kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>		    April 04	 March 21</p>
<p>		   ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p> LON-BKK	  1.13	     1.11</p>
<p> LON-HKG	  1.18	     1.16</p>
<p> LON-JAK	  1.10	     1.10</p>
<p> LON-MNL	  1.42	     1.40</p>
<p> LON-NRT	  1.95	     1.95</p>
<p> LON-PEK	  1.45	     -</p>
<p> LON-SEL	  1.87	     1.90</p>
<p> LON-SIN	  1.19	     1.19</p>
<p> LON-SYD	  2.00	     2.08</p>
<p> LON-TPE	  1.25	     1.18</p>
<p>		  MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p> LON-BAH	  0.93	     0.90</p>
<p> LON-CAI	  0.83	     0.81</p>
<p> LON-DXB	  0.80	     0.80</p>
<p>		 INDIAN SUB-CONTINENT</p>
<p> LON-BOM	  0.73	     0.73</p>
<p> LON-DEL	  0.70	     0.66</p>
<p> LON-KHI	  1.09	     1.07</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices are quoted in sterling per kg.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative or current market activity. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
